['Certainly! Below is a C code example demonstrating how to use the `open()` function with the specified flags (`O_CREAT`, `O_TRUNC`, `O_WRONLY`, and `O_EXCL`). This code attempts to create a new file or open it for writing, ensuring that if the file already exists, an error will be reported instead of overwriting or truncating it.

```c
#include <fcntl.h>  // For O_* constants
#include <sys/stat.h>  // For mode_t
